Author: Clifford Yapp <238416+starseeker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: 2026-11-12T13:35:54Z
Parents: 1778030f63d4dc4f161c1a9c3f40d459c0ff5128
Message:
    Preserve procedural hits from offset secondary rays

    Procedural child rays can begin at an offset parent point.
    Reconstructing their hits from the original ray origin moves exit points
    inside closed objects and causes repeated self-intersections.

    Keep the actual object-space hit as primary intersection data, including
    copied and side-flipped shading points and sampled surfaces. Compare
    nearest hits in the original world ray parameter and refine subsequent
    offsets from the preserved point.

    A transformed slab regression reproduces the displaced hit and failed
    escape before the fix. The complete renderer suite passes 203 suites,
    1675 cases, and 466329 assertions. Rebuild consumers against the updated
    ShadingPoint layout.

